              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a market, then the Urdu for a police station."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: محل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "محل — mahal — \"a palace\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "محل (mahal) is a loan from Arabic maḥall, \"a place of alighting, a quarter\", which reached Urdu through Persian. Its Arabic root is ḥ-l-l (Lane). In Urdu it came to mean \"a palace\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
